ASCII stays as it is:
  Lunch on Friday
only the words that need it are encoded (here Q is shorter):
  =?UTF-8?Q?=C3=84rger_mit_der_Rechnung_f=C3=BCr?= Mai
all non-Latin (B):
  =?UTF-8?B?5pel5pys6Kqe44Gu44OG44K544OI?=
a long text is cut into words of at most 75 characters:
  =?UTF-8?Q?Gr=C3=BC=C3=9Fe_aus_M=C3=BCnchen_und_dem_restlichen_Bayern=2C_m?= =?UTF-8?Q?it_vielen_weiteren_sch=C3=B6nen?= Worten dahinter
Latin-1 and UTF-8 words in one text:
  André and ü
the blank between two words is dropped:
  ab and c
a character split over two words is joined:
  Ä
an unknown character set stays as it is:
  =?x-klingon?Q?qapla=27?=
on the wire:
  From: =?UTF-8?B?TcO8bGxlciwgQW5u?= <ann@example.org>
  Subject: =?UTF-8?B?R3LDvMOfZQ==?=
decoded:
  Subject: Grüße
  From: name [Müller, Ann], address [ann@example.org]
